    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d153">

                <pb facs="0234" n="168" sameAs="frus:frus1934v05/pg168"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.3731/990: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Cuba</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Matthews</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Habana</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1934-08-23T20:00:00-05:00">August 23, 1934—8
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 8:13 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>443. Department’s telegram No. 175, August 23, 11 a.m. [<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >noon</hi>].<anchor n="71" xml:id="d153-f1"/> Cuban authorities do not
                    concur in changes listed in paragraphs 1, 2, 3, 4, 6, 8, 9, and 10, and state
                    that these changes will not therefore appear in the decree law.</p>
                <p>The President now proposes to sign the decree law tomorrow morning at 10:30.
                    However, it will be physically impossible to publish <pb facs="0235" n="169"
                        xml:id="pg169"/> the decree law in the <hi rendition="#italic">Official
                        Gazette</hi> before Saturday at the earliest. No decree law is binding until
                    published in the <hi rendition="#italic">Official Gazette.</hi></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Matthews</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d153-f1" n="71" xml:id="d153-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed; it conveyed proposed changes in the Spanish nomenclature or schedule
                    I (611.3731/986c).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
